WEBVTT

00:00:01.326 --> 00:00:02.952
[YELLS]

00:00:02.952 --> 00:00:04.287
[GRUNTING]

00:00:04.287 --> 00:00:06.247
♪ Got some cash Bought some wheels ♪

00:00:06.247 --> 00:00:10.001
[GRUNTING, SHOUTING]

00:00:10.001 --> 00:00:13.338
♪ Lost control Hit a wall ♪

00:00:13.338 --> 00:00:15.549
♪ But we're all right ♪

00:00:15.549 --> 00:00:18.176
[HAIR DRYER WHIRRING] [YELLING]

00:00:18.176 --> 00:00:23.890
♪ Are we like you? I can't be sure ♪

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:26.643
♪ Of the scene ♪

00:00:26.643 --> 00:00:28.228
[YELLING]

00:00:30.938 --> 00:00:32.357
BARNABAS: Run!

00:00:32.357 --> 00:00:33.817
♪ We run green ♪

00:00:33.817 --> 00:00:34.860
[GRUNTING]

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:36.862
MOTHER: Hey!

00:00:38.029 --> 00:00:39.656
Get back here!

00:00:39.656 --> 00:00:42.116
♪ And feel all right ♪

00:00:43.951 --> 00:00:46.287
I can't believe this is happening!

00:00:47.497 --> 00:00:50.458
[GRUNTING]

00:00:50.458 --> 00:00:52.168
[ALL GASPING]

00:00:53.336 --> 00:00:55.171
♪ Lost control Hit a wall ♪

00:00:55.171 --> 00:00:56.172
[YELLS]

00:00:56.172 --> 00:00:58.675
♪ But we're all right ♪

00:00:58.675 --> 00:01:00.968
[GRUNTING]

00:01:00.968 --> 00:01:02.763
♪ But we're all right ♪

00:01:02.763 --> 00:01:05.139
Need that altered, madam?

00:01:08.226 --> 00:01:11.772
You were amazing, kid. How'd you know how to do all that?

00:01:11.772 --> 00:01:14.482
It's a gift. Terrible at foreign languages,

00:01:14.482 --> 00:01:16.109
great at cartoon violence.

00:01:16.109 --> 00:01:20.071
Well, you did good, amigo. Sorry, I did good, a-what now?

00:01:20.071 --> 00:01:22.490
This is the best take we've had in a long time.

00:01:22.490 --> 00:01:24.367
And we got Peter to thank for it.

00:01:24.367 --> 00:01:28.329
He's the kid, the kid! Who's the kid? He's the kid.

00:01:28.329 --> 00:01:30.957
Come here, you. Come here, you! Ha, ha, ha!

00:01:30.957 --> 00:01:32.959
Hello. Knock, knock. Ding-dong.

00:01:32.959 --> 00:01:35.587
Word on the street is, you had a nice little pickup.

00:01:35.587 --> 00:01:38.840
Get lost, Robinson. Okeydokey. Will do.

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:41.468
Hope I don't blab to anyone about this though.

00:01:41.468 --> 00:01:43.344
You know how I love to blab.

00:01:43.344 --> 00:01:45.012
[CHUCKLING]

00:01:45.012 --> 00:01:46.890
Take care of him, son.

00:01:46.890 --> 00:01:48.391
Uh, sure. What can I get you?

00:01:48.391 --> 00:01:50.602
We have cheese, apples, champagne.

00:01:50.602 --> 00:01:52.938
"Congratulating..." No.

00:01:52.938 --> 00:01:54.689
Take care of him.

00:01:54.689 --> 00:01:55.941
What?

00:01:55.941 --> 00:01:57.651
No, I was kidding, Barnabas.

00:01:57.651 --> 00:01:59.444
I won't tell on you. I promise!

00:01:59.444 --> 00:02:00.946
You got to make it tight.

00:02:00.946 --> 00:02:03.531
The rabbit comes out of the hole, round the tree,

00:02:03.531 --> 00:02:06.326
back down the hole. What are you doing? No, no.

00:02:06.326 --> 00:02:07.535
No. Ugh!

00:02:07.535 --> 00:02:08.787
[ROBINSON YELLS]

00:02:08.787 --> 00:02:11.289
Hang on. Ow! That hurt, mate. Okay, son.

00:02:11.289 --> 00:02:13.667
Now take care of him. ROBINSON: No, no, no.

00:02:13.667 --> 00:02:15.084
Please stop. No, I don't...

00:02:15.084 --> 00:02:17.170
He won't say anything. Right?

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:20.089
No, no, I won't say nothing. I mean, I still feel bad

00:02:20.089 --> 00:02:21.549
about what I did to that mom.

00:02:21.549 --> 00:02:23.802
Freezer door, champagne, hair dryer.

00:02:23.802 --> 00:02:25.470
I thought that was a bit cruel.

00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:27.388
Are you part of the gang or not?

00:02:27.388 --> 00:02:30.809
Well, yeah, I'd like to be, but I don't do this.

00:02:30.809 --> 00:02:33.854
Can't we just talk it out? Please, please!

00:02:33.854 --> 00:02:35.313
No, no! Please!

00:02:35.313 --> 00:02:36.356
We're kidding!

00:02:36.356 --> 00:02:37.565
[ALL LAUGHING]

00:02:37.565 --> 00:02:39.693
We were all just playing with you.

00:02:39.693 --> 00:02:42.362
You should've seen your face, son.

00:02:42.362 --> 00:02:44.865
No, I was kidding you, so, ha-ha!

00:02:44.865 --> 00:02:46.741
You're the ones who should be wondering

00:02:46.741 --> 00:02:48.994
whether there's a private space you can go to,

00:02:48.994 --> 00:02:50.954
to check whether you've wet yourselves.

00:02:50.954 --> 00:02:52.455
[ALL LAUGHING]

00:02:52.455 --> 00:02:54.708
We share with our friends.

00:02:54.708 --> 00:02:57.502
Besides, it's gonna go bad before we can eat it all.

00:02:58.127 --> 00:02:59.880
Pigs can fly!

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:01.589
Come on. Let's get some air.

00:03:01.589 --> 00:03:05.343
♪ Three nights at the motel Under streetlights... ♪

00:03:05.343 --> 00:03:07.387
Oh, they were special times.

00:03:07.387 --> 00:03:10.640
Food enough for everyone, wide open spaces.

00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:13.351
Until old McGregor came and put that wall up.

00:03:13.351 --> 00:03:16.938
We all thought it was the end for us. But not your dad.

00:03:16.938 --> 00:03:19.774
Now, the question is: Was he stealing,

00:03:19.774 --> 00:03:22.485
or was he just taking what was already his?

00:03:22.485 --> 00:03:24.153
Exactly. We were there first.

00:03:24.153 --> 00:03:25.739
It belonged-- He was stealing.

00:03:25.739 --> 00:03:27.949
Oh. He was keeping your bellies full

00:03:27.949 --> 00:03:29.325
the only way he could.

00:03:29.325 --> 00:03:32.037
And he taught me everything I know.

00:03:32.037 --> 00:03:33.538
Fancy a treat?

00:03:33.538 --> 00:03:35.790
♪ Three nights At the motel... ♪

00:03:35.790 --> 00:03:37.500
Wait here.

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:39.377
♪ In the city of Palms ♪

00:03:39.377 --> 00:03:42.463
♪ Call me what you want When you want, if you want ♪

00:03:42.463 --> 00:03:44.257
♪ Don't waste a minute... ♪

00:03:44.257 --> 00:03:46.175
Coming at you! Aah!

00:03:46.175 --> 00:03:47.802
Here you go, son.

00:03:47.802 --> 00:03:50.638
Wow, that's so good. What is this?

00:03:50.638 --> 00:03:52.223
It's a potato.

00:03:52.223 --> 00:03:55.727
What?!

00:03:55.727 --> 00:03:57.979
Let me ask a question. Is my voice annoying?

00:03:57.979 --> 00:04:00.815
Yeah, it's a bit polarizing, but I like it.

00:04:00.815 --> 00:04:04.193
I love this place. No one telling me I'm bad.

00:04:04.193 --> 00:04:06.237
I really feel like I belong.

00:04:06.237 --> 00:04:08.197
I wish I had 10 more just like you.

00:04:08.197 --> 00:04:09.574
Then I could pull off the job

00:04:09.574 --> 00:04:11.367
me and your dad used to dream about.

00:04:11.367 --> 00:04:14.161
One that could feed us forever. BEA: Peter!

00:04:14.161 --> 00:04:15.204
THOMAS: Peter?

00:04:15.204 --> 00:04:16.998
Come on. BEA: Peter!

00:04:16.998 --> 00:04:19.751
Peter! There you are.

00:04:19.751 --> 00:04:22.879
BEA: Oh, Peter. We've been looking all over for you.

00:04:22.879 --> 00:04:24.589
Oh, thank goodness. Are you okay?

00:04:24.589 --> 00:04:27.592
He's fine. We have to hurry to catch the last train.

00:04:27.592 --> 00:04:29.427
Okay.

00:04:29.427 --> 00:04:31.721
[VAMPIRE WEEKEND'S "HARMONY HALL" PLAYING]

00:04:32.806 --> 00:04:33.848
[CLICKS TONGUE]

00:04:35.516 --> 00:04:37.685
BENJAMIN: Peter, what happened to you?

00:04:37.685 --> 00:04:39.854
We were starting to get worried.

00:04:39.854 --> 00:04:43.399
I just went for a walk. Come on, let's go.

00:04:43.399 --> 00:04:44.776
Is he all right?

00:04:44.776 --> 00:04:46.736
Seems to be.

00:04:46.736 --> 00:04:47.862
[SNORING]

00:04:47.862 --> 00:04:49.781
♪ We took a vow in summertime ♪

00:04:49.781 --> 00:04:53.868
♪ Now we find ourselves In late December ♪

00:04:57.246 --> 00:04:59.248
♪ Anger wants a voice... ♪

00:04:59.248 --> 00:05:00.917
[THOMAS PANTING]

00:05:00.917 --> 00:05:02.836
THOMAS: Yes! Yes.

00:05:02.836 --> 00:05:06.047
What are you doing? Ooh! Doing some push-ups.

00:05:06.047 --> 00:05:09.509
Oh, you just suddenly had the urge to work out, did you?

00:05:09.509 --> 00:05:12.178
Just suddenly had the urge to read Dickens, did you?

00:05:12.178 --> 00:05:13.847
You know he's my favorite author.

00:05:13.847 --> 00:05:16.599
Name another book by Dickens.

00:05:16.599 --> 00:05:18.143
Do another push-up.

00:05:19.519 --> 00:05:20.520
Okay.

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:21.938
[GRUNTING]

00:05:23.397 --> 00:05:25.191
[WHIMPERING]

00:05:28.111 --> 00:05:30.279
Oh, I'm stuck. I'm stuck.

00:05:30.279 --> 00:05:32.949
[INSECTS CHIRPING]

00:05:32.949 --> 00:05:34.993
Cock-a-doodle-do!

00:05:34.993 --> 00:05:38.245
Wake up, kids! Wake up! We have a job to do!

00:05:38.245 --> 00:05:39.330
What? Dad.

00:05:39.330 --> 00:05:40.957
Come on. We're tired.

00:05:40.957 --> 00:05:43.668
But we have to make the gigantic ball of fire

00:05:43.668 --> 00:05:46.754
rise into the sky so the earth gets warm

00:05:46.754 --> 00:05:49.340
and life as we know it can continue!

00:05:49.340 --> 00:05:50.717
What? For real?

00:05:50.717 --> 00:05:52.343
That's a lot of responsibility.

00:05:52.343 --> 00:05:54.637
ALL: Cock-a-doodle-do!

00:05:54.637 --> 00:05:56.681
ALL [QUIETLY]: Cock-a-doodle-do.

00:05:56.681 --> 00:05:58.975
Now, feel free to peck around,

00:05:58.975 --> 00:06:02.854
doing absolutely nothing for the next 24 hours.

00:06:02.854 --> 00:06:04.898
[♪♪♪]

00:06:04.898 --> 00:06:07.734
[BEA LAUGHING]

00:06:07.734 --> 00:06:10.319
BENJAMIN: Ready to tell me where you went yesterday?

00:06:10.319 --> 00:06:13.280
You had us all worried. No need to worry, cousin.

00:06:13.280 --> 00:06:15.950
I was meeting someone who may have changed my life.

00:06:15.950 --> 00:06:18.285
[GASPS, GRUNTS]

